   "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
   "check_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
   "summary": "All of these commenters respond to the anesthesia supervision request for information and urge CMS to drop the federal physician supervision requirement for nurse anesthetists. They argue the requirement lacks a statutory basis, that many states have already opted out, and that research shows no safety or outcome difference without supervision. They say the rule restricts access to anesthesia, particularly in rural and underserved areas, and raises costs by forcing duplicate staffing. A few add personal accounts of supervision being purely a billing formality, or argue that collaboration should follow clinical judgment rather than a federal mandate.",
