   "summary": "All of the sampled comments are the same form letter, and all of them ask DHS to withdraw the interim final rule and restore the 30-day response window for refugees facing a notice of intent to terminate. They argue that ten days, counted from the mailing date rather than the receipt date, is too little time to understand a legal notice, find a lawyer, and collect evidence from countries the refugees fled. They stress the severe consequences: loss of status and work authorization, possible removal proceedings, effects on family members, and no appeal. They also say DHS has not justified the change, since the process has been stable for decades and the agency can already pursue removal directly. One version adds a religious appeal to treat refugees as fellow human beings.",
